      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/fsh-guts.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "`fsh-guts/` — the trashcan that is kept",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-19:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/fsh-guts.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why the never-delete rule needed a destination",
      "prov:value": "`AGENTS.md` has always forbidden deleting a bean, and its reason was never\nabout beans:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/fsh-guts.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why the never-delete rule needed a destination",
      "prov:value": "1. Work that is wanted but wrong → fix it.\n2. Work that is not wanted → **move it to `fsh-guts/`**, with a note saying\n   what superseded it. Since 2026-10-04 that means the MOUNTED copy, pushed\n   to its branch — see §\"Where it lives\", below.\n3. Actual deletion → **only on explicit confirmation from the owner**, asked\n   for as a question, never inferred from \"this is obviously dead\".",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/fsh-guts.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why the never-delete rule needed a destination",
      "prov:value": "## Where it lives — its own branch, mounted at `fsh-guts/` (bean `9c7h`)",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 9c7h"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/fsh-guts.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where it lives — its own branch, mounted at `fsh-guts/` (bean `9c7h`)",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-02: *\"fsh-guts content gets its own named branch,\ncat/cat-harness/fsh-guts, and the contents of fsh-guts/ dir goes there.\"*\nSince the 2026-10-04 cutover the trashcan is **not on `main`**. Its\ndeclaration says `source: { kind: \"branch\", branch: \"cat/cat-harness/fsh-guts\",\nkeyedBy: \"tip\" }`, and `main` ignores the directory (`/fsh-guts/**`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-02",
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02",
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/fsh-guts.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where it lives — its own branch, mounted at `fsh-guts/` (bean `9c7h`)",
      "prov:value": "- **Never `git add -f` anything under `fsh-guts/` to `main`.** That makes a\n  second copy that diverges from the branch. The ignore rule is there to stop\n  `git add -A` from doing it by accident.\n- **An unmounted `fsh-guts/` is not an empty trashcan.** Every reader (the\n  export, the visualiser, `check:uploads-retired`, `check:retired-front-matter`)\n  asks `contentAt(\"fsh-guts\")` and exits 2, \"could not determine\", instead of\n  reporting a clean, empty corpus. CI mounts before it reads.\n- **`fsh-guts/logs/` stays local scratch.** It is never pushed, and logs\n  written before the first mount do not block the mount.\n- **There is no viewer page to commit after a relocation.** The page\n  `cat-harness/docs/fsh-guts/index.md` is derived from this branch, so it is\n  built at publish by `derive:publish` and gitignored (bean `0b8c`, #2230).\n  Before that it was committed, and one relocation made it stale on main and\n  on every open PR at once (2026-10-05). `fsh-guts:viz:check` now judges that\n  the mounted graph renders. The rule is general:\n  [`directory-conventions`](directory-conventions.md) §\"The storage clock\".",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 0b8c",
        "#2230",
        "2026-10-05"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/fsh-guts.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "It is exported, and it is not rendered — and it is not in the KG either",
      "prov:value": "- served as `<base>/fsh-guts.jsonld`, alongside the instance's other\n  renderings, so a consumer can walk it **by name** — built by\n  `scripts/fsh-guts-export.ts`, published by `docs-site.yml`, with a\n  `.json` alias because Pages has no media type for `.jsonld` and serves it\n  as octet-stream. **Logs are excluded by DECLARATION**: a file is included\n  only if it says `$schema: folio-fsh-guts/v1`, so a log entry is left out\n  because of what it says it is, not because `.gitignore` kept it off the\n  build machine — which is a property of the checkout and not of the export\n- **absent from the site build** — this is the property, not a side effect.\n  A change that causes `fsh-guts/` to render has broken it\n- **stripped from every other published graph.** Owner, 2026-09-19: *\"NEVER\n  include fsh-guts, references to fsh-guts stripped out of KG before sending\n  to publication.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/fsh-guts.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "It is exported, and it is not rendered — and it is not in the KG either",
      "prov:value": "**Those last two are different properties and the second is easy to miss.**\nKeeping the CONTENT out of the render pipeline does not keep the REFERENCE\nout of the graph: an instance's declared directories become nodes in\n`<stub>.jsonld`, so declaring this directory — required, or nothing can find\nit — put its id, path and description into the published document. That was\nshipped and then corrected the same day."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/fsh-guts.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "It is exported, and it is not rendered — and it is not in the KG either",
      "prov:value": "A consumer may fetch `fsh-guts.jsonld` deliberately. It must never **arrive**\nthere by following an edge. Mechanism and the three emitters that had to be\nfiltered: [`kg-export`](kg-export.md) §\"`fsh-guts` NEVER reaches a published\ngraph\". Where this sits among everything else the site publishes, and what\nelse is never published: [`instance-publication`](instance-publication.md)\n§\"What each instance publishes\"."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/fsh-guts.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "It is exported, and it is not rendered — and it is not in the KG either",
      "prov:value": "Reaching it as a human is the dead-fish icon under settings, with a node\ncounter and a select dialog. Bean `folio-assistant-7vhe`; until that exists,\nthe files are reachable through the repository and the JSON-LD.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean folio-assistant-7vhe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/fsh-guts.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "On the name",
      "prov:value": "`.fsh` is **FHIR Shorthand** — in the DAK layer's `schemas/dak.ts`, `jsonld.ts`,\n`translation-tools.ts`, `block-qa.ts`, and throughout the WHO SMART folios\nthis platform targets. The overlap was raised and the owner confirmed this\nspelling anyway."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/fsh-guts.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "On the name",
      "prov:value": "## An INGESTED SOURCE comes here — owner, 2026-09-29",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ]
    }
